160
00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:03.690
They spend hours planning parties.
他们花好几个小时策划派对。

161
00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:05.030
Excuse me, guys.
打扰一下，伙计们。

162
00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:07.610
What's going on in here?
这里面在搞什么？

163
00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:09.750
Party planning committee, not your concern, Charles.
派对策划委员会的事，跟你没关系，查尔斯。

164
00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:12.570
This doesn't seem like a good way to spend company time.
这看起来可不是打发公司时间的好方法。

165
00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:13.110
Really?
是吗？

166
00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:16.890
Well, then how would we come up with great ideas like Jim's?
那我们怎么能想出像吉姆那样棒的点子呢？

167
00:06:17.170 --> 00:06:17.630
Go ahead.
说吧。

168
00:06:17.890 --> 00:06:19.530
No, I'd like to get back to work, actually.
不，其实我想回去工作了。

169
00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:20.250
What you got, Jim?
你有什么想法，吉姆？

170
00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:23.790
What is a two-way petting zoo?
什么是双向动物园？

171
00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:28.570
Okay.
好吧。

172
00:06:29.510 --> 00:06:30.310
That's amazing.
太绝了。

173
00:06:30.630 --> 00:06:32.710
So, I just have to ask you, lady.
所以，我不得不问你，女士。

174
00:06:33.350 --> 00:06:35.890
I mean, was it so hard not to laugh?
我是说，忍住不笑是不是很难？

175
00:06:36.030 --> 00:06:37.950
Because Idris Elba is playing it so straight.
因为伊德瑞斯·艾尔巴演得太正经了。

176
00:06:38.090 --> 00:06:38.450
Yes.
对。

177
00:06:38.650 --> 00:06:40.510
And he's like, what's a two-way petting zoo?
而且他就像是在问，什么是双向动物园？

178
00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:43.270
Like, it must have been so hard not to break.
就觉得，当时要忍住不笑场一定超级难。

179
00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:46.790
It was really also very hard for me to say that line.
说真的，我要说出那句台词也非常难。

180
00:06:46.790 --> 00:06:49.310
It's just strippers and cakes all the way down.
从头到尾全都是脱衣舞女和蛋糕。

181
00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:52.170
That is such a beautifully written line.
这台词写得实在太妙了。

182
00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:55.890
It's, oh, chef's kiss to the writer who wrote that.
简直是，哦，对写出这句台词的编剧致以厨神之吻。

183
00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:59.730
And then, yes, what is a two-way petting zoo?
然后，对啊，什么是双向动物园？

184
00:07:00.290 --> 00:07:02.230
Yes, it was very hard not to laugh.
对，要忍住不笑真的很难。

185
00:07:02.230 --> 00:07:02.870
It was.
确实很难。

186
00:07:03.470 --> 00:07:07.210
And Phyllis, man, talk about just in the corner plotting, man.
还有菲利斯，天呐，简直就是在角落里密谋呢。

187
00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:09.050
All right.
好了。

188
00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:13.930
Well, listen, everyone, we hope you enjoy your second drink of New Boss.
那么听着，各位，我们希望你们喜欢你们的第二杯《新老板》。

189
00:07:18.130 --> 00:07:19.070
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

190
00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:20.390
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金西。

191
00:07:20.510 --> 00:07:21.670
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演过《办公室》。

192
00:07:21.910 --> 00:07:22.910
And we're best friends.
我们是最好的朋友。

193
00:07:22.910 --> 00:07:26.750
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在我们专门为你带来《办公室》终极重温播客。

194
00:07:26.890 --> 00:07:31.450
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories
每周，我们将剖析一集《办公室》，并分享独家幕后故事，

195
00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:33.730
that only two people who were there can tell you.
只有身临其境的两个人才能告诉你。

196
00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:34.870
We're The Office Ladies.
我们是办公室女士。

197
00:07:34.870 --> 00:07:42.020
Good morning, good afternoon, good evening.
早上好，下午好，晚上好。

198
00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:43.360
You did it.
你做到了。

199
00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:44.180
You covered it all.
你全都覆盖到了。

200
00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:45.040
Did I get everybody?
我是不是把所有人都照顾到了？

201
00:07:45.260 --> 00:07:45.780
You did.
你确实说过。

202
00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:49.700
This week, we're talking about New Boss.
本周我们讨论的是《新老板》这一集。

203
00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:52.240
I was delighted by this episode.
我对这一集感到非常惊喜。

204
00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:53.040
Me too.
我也是。

205
00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:54.400
I read the script.
我读了剧本。

206
00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:57.260
I read the script, and I was cackling.
我读了剧本，当时笑得合不拢嘴。

207
00:07:57.540 --> 00:07:58.680
Josh was like, what are you reading?
乔希当时问：你在看什么？

208
00:07:58.780 --> 00:08:01.160
I'm like, it's the shooting draft for New Boss.
我说：这是《新老板》的拍摄剧本。

209
00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:04.360
It was so good.
真的太棒了。

210
00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:07.800
This was Season 5, Episode 20.
这是第五季第二十集。

211
00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:13.300
It was written by Lee Eisenberg and Gene Stupnitsky and directed by Paul Feig.
由李·艾森伯格和吉恩·斯图普尼斯基编剧，保罗·费格执导。

212
00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:14.880
Hit me with a summary.
给我讲讲剧情概要。

213
00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:15.700
I will.
好的。

214
00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:19.080
There is a new boss at corporate.
公司来了一位新老板。

215
00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:26.320
They filled the position that used to be held by Jan, and then Ryan, with new regional supervisor,
他们填补了之前由简和瑞恩担任的职位，新来的地区主管是

216
00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:27.800
Charles Minor.
查尔斯·迈纳。

217
00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:30.680
And he's coming to Scranton for a visit.
他要来斯克兰顿视察。

218
00:08:30.980 --> 00:08:33.040
He's going to hobnob with us all day.
他要跟我们混上一整天。

219
00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:33.600
Yeah.
对。

220
00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:41.620
He is also going to announce some new policies involving our budget, in particular, our party budget.
他还将宣布一些关于我们预算的新政策，特别是我们的派对预算。

221
00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:46.980
Well, to be fair to the new boss, Michael was supposed to let us know.
嗯，平心而论，本来该由迈克尔通知我们的。

222
00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:48.240
He was.
本该如此。

223
00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:50.600
But once again, he did not.
但又一次，他没有这么做。

224
00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:55.860
And instead, he started planning his own 15th anniversary party.
相反，他开始筹划自己的十五周年纪念派对。

225
00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:59.640
He's been working at Dunder Mifflin for 15 years, and he wants to have a big party.
他在邓德米夫林工作了十五年，想要办一场盛大的派对。

226
00:08:59.860 --> 00:09:01.020
Big, big party.
非常、非常盛大的派对。

227
00:09:01.760 --> 00:09:04.120
Things do not go well with Michael and Charles.
迈克尔和查尔斯相处得并不愉快。

228
00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:05.860
Or with Jim and Charles.
吉姆和查尔斯也是如此。

229
00:09:06.140 --> 00:09:07.600
Oh, that was so fun.
哦，那太有意思了。

230
00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:11.500
It's maybe one of my favorite runners ever.
这可能是我最喜欢的贯穿情节之一了。

231
00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:19.080
Watching Jim be sort of like on the outs with someone and feeling like embarrassed was so good.
看着吉姆和某人有点疏离又感到尴尬，真是太精彩了。

232
00:09:19.380 --> 00:09:21.400
So, so fun.
太有意思了。

233
00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:23.640
Michael is spinning out.
迈克尔情绪失控了。

234
00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:25.840
He tries to get David Wallace on the phone.
他试图给大卫·华莱士打电话。

235
00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:32.600
He can't, so he drives to New York, where things are going to take a dramatic turn.
打不通，于是他开车去了纽约，在那里事情将迎来戏剧性的转折。

236
00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:33.520
Bum, bum, bum.
咚，咚，咚。

237
00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:35.540
Fast fact number one.
趣事第一条。

238
00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:36.220
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

239
00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:38.220
I mentioned there's a new boss in town.
我提到镇里来了一位新老板。

240
00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:41.260
Oh, please give me the character breakdown.
哦，请给我介绍一下这个角色吧。

241
00:09:41.800 --> 00:09:44.580
That person is Idris Elba.
那个演员是伊德瑞斯·艾尔巴。

242
00:09:44.900 --> 00:09:45.160
Yep.
没错。

243
00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:46.280
All right.
好的。

244
00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:47.360
Yes, it is.
是的，就是他。

245
00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:49.140
Let's get this out of the way.
我们先把这个放一边。

246
00:09:49.140 --> 00:09:51.740
Let's just roll up our sleeves and talk about Idris for a second.
我们卷起袖子，花点时间聊聊伊德瑞斯吧。

247
00:09:53.020 --> 00:09:56.380
Idris is the most beautiful man I have ever laid my eyes on.
伊德瑞斯是我见过最帅的男人。

248
00:09:57.120 --> 00:09:57.840
He is.
确实如此。

249
00:09:58.180 --> 00:10:01.980
And I want to say I've laid my eyes on some gentleman, famous gentleman.
我想说我见过的绅士、出名的绅士也不少。

250
00:10:02.180 --> 00:10:02.480
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

251
00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:04.020
He's not just beautiful.
他不仅仅是长得好看。

252
00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:07.820
There is just, I don't know how to explain it, you guys.
就是那种，我不知道该怎么解释，伙计们。

253
00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:11.440
When, you know those people that walk in a room and you just go, damn.
当，你知道那种人，走进一个房间，你就会忍不住说，天哪。

254
00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:12.940
It's a whole aura.
那是一种整体的气场。

255
00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:13.700
Yeah.
没错。

256
00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:14.740
It's a presence.
这是一种存在感。

257
00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:18.980
We got a fan question from Anna B and Allie C.
我们收到了来自安娜·B和艾莉·C的粉丝提问。

258
00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:21.500
How did Idris Elba end up on the show?
伊德瑞斯·艾尔巴怎么会来演这部剧的？

259
00:10:21.740 --> 00:10:26.320
Randy told me that the role of Charles Minor was written for Idris.
兰迪告诉我，查尔斯·迈纳这个角色就是为伊德瑞斯量身写的。

260
00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:29.280
He is the only person they ever approached for the role.
他是他们为这个角色接洽的唯一人选。

261
00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:35.020
He said that Idris's name was in the story outline for this episode, which comes out like
他说伊德瑞斯的名字出现在这一集的剧情大纲里，那大概是在

262
00:10:35.020 --> 00:10:37.100
two months before you even shoot it.
你甚至开拍前两个月就出来了。

263
00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:38.780
And he even sent it to me.
而且他还把它发给了我。

264
00:10:38.960 --> 00:10:44.820
It says, interior reception, Charles Minor, comma, Idris enters.
上面写着，内景前台，查尔斯·迈纳，逗号，伊德瑞斯登场。

265
00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:48.620
Like, they were like, we want Idris Elba for this role.
就像是，他们当时说，我们就要伊德瑞斯·艾尔巴来演这个角色。

266
00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:51.420
Oh my gosh, they were planning this pretty far out.
哦天哪，他们筹划得相当早。

267
00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:51.780
Yeah.
是啊。

268
00:10:52.140 --> 00:10:55.600
Well, the writing staff was a really huge fan of the TV show, The Wire.
嗯，编剧团队真的是电视剧《火线》的超级粉丝。

269
00:10:55.780 --> 00:10:56.640
That's what I was going to say.
正是我要说的。

270
00:10:56.740 --> 00:10:58.440
We had a lot of The Wire fans.
我们有很多《火线》的粉丝。

271
00:10:58.880 --> 00:10:59.880
Do you remember that show?
你还记得那部剧吗？

272
00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:01.500
Everybody was so obsessed with it.
所有人都对它着迷不已。

273
00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:02.400
It's such a great show.
那真是一部伟大的剧。

274
00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:02.620
Yeah.
对啊。

275
00:11:02.840 --> 00:11:05.140
And to get Stringer Bell, come on.
能请到斯特林·贝尔，简直绝了。

276
00:11:05.340 --> 00:11:06.020
I know.
我懂的。

277
00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:11.300
Well, he's the second cast member we've had from The Wire because Amy Ryan was also on The Wire.
嗯，他是我们剧组迎来的第二位出自《火线》的演员，因为艾米·莱恩也演过《火线》。

278
00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:11.560
Yep.
没错。

279
00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:24.040
Who have one accent in real life, but have to speak in a different accent for the role.
现实生活中有一种口音，但为了角色却不得不说另一种口音。

280
00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:30.040
Did Idris Elba speak in his normal British accent between takes, or did he stay in character
伊德瑞斯·艾尔巴在拍片间隙是用他平常的英国口音说话，还是全程

281
00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:32.140
with his American accent the whole time?
都保持着美式口音的角色状态？

282
00:11:32.560 --> 00:11:36.600
Yeah, I guess we should mention Idris has a British accent.
对，我想我们应该提一下，伊德瑞斯有英国口音。

283
00:11:37.020 --> 00:11:40.140
Which pretty much wrecked us all.
这简直把我们迷得神魂颠倒。

284
00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:41.600
Yeah.
是啊。

285
00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:48.140
I mean, if you look like Idris and then you sound like Idris, what were we supposed to do?
我的意思是，如果你长得像伊德瑞斯，说话又像伊德瑞斯，我们能怎么办呢？

286
00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:50.380
We were all so charmed by him.
我们所有人都被他迷住了。

287
00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:51.840
So charmed.
迷得神魂颠倒。

288
00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:55.040
And yes, he did speak in his British accent between takes.
没错，他在拍片间隙确实是用英国口音说话的。

289
00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:55.900
Right.
对的。

290
00:11:56.460 --> 00:11:59.580
Fast fact number two, more Idris Elba.
速记冷知识之二，更多关于伊德瑞斯·艾尔巴的内容。

291
00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:00.180
Okay.
好的。

292
00:12:00.420 --> 00:12:00.940
I'm sorry.
不好意思。

293
00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:02.160
He's too great.
他太棒了。

294
00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:03.660
We're going to keep talking about him.
我们要继续聊他。

295
00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:10.040
As you know, since being on The Wire and The Office, he has gone on to do a gazillion things,
如你所知，自从演了《火线》和《办公室》之后，他后来接了无数的工作，

296
00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:11.280
movies, TV shows.
电影、电视剧。

297
00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:13.380
He was most recently in The Suicide Squad.
他最近出演了《X特遣队：全员集结》。

298
00:12:13.780 --> 00:12:15.200
But did you know this?
但你知道这个吗？

299
00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:16.800
Because I didn't know this.
因为我之前不知道。

300
00:12:17.440 --> 00:12:19.880
Before he was an actor, he was a DJ.
在他成为演员之前，他是一名DJ。

301
00:12:20.900 --> 00:12:21.160
Okay.
好吧。

302
00:12:21.320 --> 00:12:22.340
I did know that.
我确实知道那个。

303
00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:27.380
I did know that probably because I was so excited he was coming.
我之所以知道大概是因为他要来我太兴奋了。

304
00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:29.080
I like looked up everything about him.
我差不多把他的一切都查了个遍。

305
00:12:29.180 --> 00:12:32.020
Just in case a topic came up, I would know something.
以防聊到什么话题时，我能接上话。

306
00:12:32.720 --> 00:12:37.180
Wait, before he was on the show, you like Googled him and you're like,
等等，在他上节目之前，你竟然去谷歌搜索他，然后心想，

307
00:12:37.300 --> 00:12:38.940
I need topics of conversation.
我需要聊天话题。

308
00:12:38.940 --> 00:12:41.100
I just want to know everything about him.
我只是想了解他的一切。

309
00:12:41.680 --> 00:12:42.060
Okay.
好吧。

310
00:12:42.060 --> 00:12:45.940
I did not Google him until we had to prep for this podcast,
直到我们要为这个播客做准备时我才去搜他，

311
00:12:46.100 --> 00:12:49.480
during which I found out that he is a big time DJ.
在这期间我发现他是个大牌DJ。

312
00:12:49.860 --> 00:12:50.060
Yeah.
对。

313
00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:52.580
Growing up, he DJed parties.
他从小就给派对当DJ。

314
00:12:52.920 --> 00:12:56.280
And when he was a struggling actor and he first came to the US,
当他还是个苦苦挣扎的演员、刚来美国时，

315
00:12:56.280 --> 00:12:58.740
it was really hard for him to get work because he had a special visa.
因为拿的是特殊签证，他很难找到工作。

316
00:12:59.080 --> 00:13:01.300
But he was able to get gigs as a DJ.
但他能接到当DJ的活儿。

317
00:13:01.620 --> 00:13:04.040
He also worked as a bouncer, which I found very interesting.
他还当过保镖，我觉得这很有意思。

318
00:13:04.040 --> 00:13:07.680
He goes by the name of DJ Big Driss.
他的艺名叫“大德里斯DJ”。

319
00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:09.940
And now he's done like tons of shows.
现在他已经演出了无数场。

320
00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:11.420
He did a party for Michael Jordan.
他给迈克尔·乔丹办过派对。

321
00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:14.640
He DJed the wedding of Prince Harry and Meghan Markle.
他给哈里王子和梅根·马克尔的婚礼当过DJ。

322
00:13:14.840 --> 00:13:16.280
That I did not know.
这个我真不知道。

323
00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:17.520
How did I miss that?
我怎么漏掉了这个？

324
00:13:17.820 --> 00:13:19.420
You need to do more Googling.
你需要多谷歌一下。

325
00:13:19.420 --> 00:13:21.160
Well, I guess I need to re-Google.
好吧，我想我得重新谷歌一下。

326
00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:21.780
Yeah.
对。

327
00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:24.420
He also played Coachello in 2019.
他还在2019年登上了科切拉音乐节。

328
00:13:24.960 --> 00:13:26.400
He got rave reviews.
他获得了极高的评价。

329
00:13:26.840 --> 00:13:30.200
And he just released a new house track through his label,
他刚刚通过自己的厂牌

330
00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:34.740
Seven Wallace, called Fudge, with vocalist Eliza Legzina.
Seven Wallace发行了一首名为《Fudge》的新浩室舞曲，合作歌手是埃莉扎·莱格齐娜。

331
00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:36.180
And I thought we should listen to it.
我觉得我们应该听听看。

332
00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:36.960
Oh, I'd love that.
哦，我很乐意。

333
00:13:55.150 --> 00:13:56.590
This man can do no wrong.
这个男人简直无可挑剔。

334
00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:57.710
He, I mean.
我是说他。

335
00:13:58.110 --> 00:13:58.670
Stop it.
别这样。

336
00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:00.850
Can we get invited to a party where he DJs?
我们能受邀去他担任DJ的派对吗？

337
00:14:00.930 --> 00:14:01.830
It'll never happen.
那绝不可能发生。

338
00:14:02.090 --> 00:14:02.770
Can we?
可以吗？

339
00:14:02.770 --> 00:14:03.850
I don't think it'll happen.
我觉得不可能发生。

340
00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:06.590
I don't think we'll make the list, but I would love it.
我觉得我们进不了名单，但我很想去。

341
00:14:06.770 --> 00:14:07.350
You know what?
你知道吗？

342
00:14:07.570 --> 00:14:07.710
We could.
我们可以的。

343
00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:09.530
Let's go hide in some bushes.
我们去灌木丛里躲着吧。

344
00:14:09.710 --> 00:14:10.290
We'll sneak in.
我们偷偷溜进去。

345
00:14:10.710 --> 00:14:11.410
Bush hiders.
灌木丛躲藏者。

346
00:14:11.510 --> 00:14:12.790
Well, bush hiders goes to.
好吧，灌木丛躲藏者去……

347
00:14:13.110 --> 00:14:15.890
Bush hiders goes to the club.
灌木丛躲藏者去夜店。

348
00:14:16.130 --> 00:14:18.790
Lady, this is like kind of one of my new life goals,
天呐，这简直成了我的人生新目标之一，

349
00:14:18.850 --> 00:14:22.590
which is to go to a party that Idris DJs.
那就是去参加一场伊德里斯担任DJ的派对。

350
00:14:22.670 --> 00:14:23.790
I want to do it.
我想去。

351
00:14:23.950 --> 00:14:24.950
And dance it up.
尽情跳舞吧。

352
00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:26.050
What do we wear?
我们穿什么？

353
00:14:26.210 --> 00:14:27.590
What do you wear to something like that?
这种场合到底该穿什么？

354
00:14:27.810 --> 00:14:29.850
Can I wear one of my fake flowers?
我能戴我的一朵假花吗？

355
00:14:30.210 --> 00:14:31.210
I'm going to say no.
我觉得不行。

356
00:14:31.370 --> 00:14:32.030
Not on this.
这个可不行。

357
00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:32.490
I agree.
我同意。

358
00:14:32.770 --> 00:14:33.170
I agree.
我同意。

359
00:14:33.530 --> 00:14:37.150
You know what show that Idris was in that my husband loved was Luther.
你知道伊德里斯演的那部我老公超爱的剧是《路德》。

360
00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:37.750
Yes.
对。

361
00:14:38.030 --> 00:14:39.270
Luther is so good.
《路德》太棒了。

362
00:14:39.390 --> 00:14:40.370
It's so good.
真的太棒了。

363
00:14:40.610 --> 00:14:46.090
He also did a show that he created himself where he plays a DJ called Turn Up Charlie.
他还演过一部他自己创作的剧，在里面饰演一个叫查理的DJ，剧名叫《查理说嗨》。

364
00:14:46.870 --> 00:14:47.990
He's done it all.
他什么都演过。

365
00:14:48.290 --> 00:14:48.830
He's done it all.
他什么都演过。

366
00:14:49.230 --> 00:14:49.770
All right.
好吧。

367
00:14:49.910 --> 00:14:50.770
I will move us on.
我来推进流程。

368
00:14:50.910 --> 00:14:53.570
Fast fact number three is not about Idris, even though it could be.
第三个趣味冷知识跟伊德里斯无关，尽管其实也可以有关。

369
00:14:54.510 --> 00:14:58.470
Fast fact number three is, why is it raining in this episode?
第三个趣味冷知识是，为什么这一集里一直在下雨？

370
00:14:58.770 --> 00:15:00.090
All throughout the episode.
整整一集都在下。

371
00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:01.030
The whole episode.
整集都在下。

372
00:15:01.150 --> 00:15:01.350
Pouring rain.
倾盆大雨。

373
00:15:01.350 --> 00:15:02.210
Not just raining.
不仅仅是下雨。

374
00:15:02.370 --> 00:15:02.830
Pouring rain.
倾盆大雨。

375
00:15:03.030 --> 00:15:05.370
So much so you can hear it in the talking heads.
雨大得在访谈镜头里都能听到声音。

376
00:15:06.030 --> 00:15:06.330
Yeah.
对。

377
00:15:06.650 --> 00:15:06.830
Yeah.
对。

378
00:15:07.190 --> 00:15:09.090
I started by looking in the script.
我一开始先去翻了剧本。

379
00:15:09.270 --> 00:15:14.410
I thought, was there a deleted something that tells us why it's raining?
我想着，是不是有什么被删掉的剧情解释了为什么下雨？

380
00:15:14.410 --> 00:15:18.970
I only found one random side comment by Michael.
我只找到了迈克尔随口说的一句闲话。

381
00:15:19.190 --> 00:15:19.650
Same.
我也是。

382
00:15:19.910 --> 00:15:23.090
It's in the scene where he's making small talk with Charles.
就在他跟查尔斯闲聊的那场戏里。

383
00:15:23.490 --> 00:15:23.770
Yep.
没错。

384
00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:27.130
And he says, so great weather we're having, huh?
他说，天气真好哈？

385
00:15:27.270 --> 00:15:29.090
Kind of rainy, you know, but still humid.
有点下雨，你知道的，但还是挺潮湿的。

386
00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:30.790
But that was it.
但也就仅此而已了。

387
00:15:30.870 --> 00:15:31.650
That is it.
真的就只有这样。

388
00:15:31.750 --> 00:15:33.970
So I asked Randy about it and here's what he said.
所以我去问了兰迪，他是这么说的。

389
00:15:34.130 --> 00:15:40.670
He said, if I recall correctly, we entered this week expecting rain all across LA.
他说，如果我没记错的话，我们开拍这一周时，整个洛杉矶预报的都是雨天。

390
00:15:41.230 --> 00:15:48.170
In fact, the top of our call sheets for the first two days of shooting say, be prepared for rain because they would do that.
事实上，前两天的通告单顶部都写着：做好防雨准备，因为剧组一贯如此。

391
00:15:48.330 --> 00:15:53.470
And then they would have extra umbrellas and like all kinds of things for us if we were shooting outside.
而且如果我们要在室外拍摄，他们就会准备额外的雨伞和各种各样的东西供我们使用。

392
00:15:54.610 --> 00:15:59.330
Randy said the very first day of shooting, we had to shoot these driving scenes with Steve.
兰迪说开拍的第一天，我们就得拍史蒂夫的这些车内戏。

393
00:16:00.010 --> 00:16:04.770
They were supposed to be Michael driving to and from his meeting with David Wallace.
本来应该是迈克尔开车去见大卫·华莱士以及开回来的过程。

394
00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:06.530
Oh, I have some.
哦，我这里有一些。

395
00:16:06.730 --> 00:16:09.070
I'm going to play later for when he leaves.
等会儿他离开的时候我要放出来。

396
00:16:09.230 --> 00:16:09.870
It's amazing.
太绝了。

397
00:16:10.050 --> 00:16:11.650
Because they got deleted, right?
因为这些被删掉了对吧？

398
00:16:11.810 --> 00:16:12.230
That's right.
没错。

399
00:16:12.470 --> 00:16:17.210
Well, I guess while they were shooting this, it was raining all over the car.
嗯，我猜他们拍这场戏的时候，车窗上到处都是雨水。

400
00:16:17.470 --> 00:16:19.110
The wipers are going and all that.
雨刮器一直在刮，诸如此类的。

401
00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:27.090
That afternoon, they moved back to our parking lot where they had to shoot the scenes of Angela and Kelly trying to find Charles.
那天下午，他们搬回了我们的停车场，在那里他们得拍摄安吉拉和凯莉试图找到查尔斯的戏份。

402
00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:29.610
That's one, Angela, where you're like gripping his scarf.
那是第一场，安吉拉，就是你抓着他围巾的那场。

403
00:16:29.790 --> 00:16:30.110
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

404
00:16:30.230 --> 00:16:30.730
In the rain.
在雨中。

405
00:16:30.850 --> 00:16:31.230
Yes.
没错。

406
00:16:31.410 --> 00:16:34.270
He said it was steadily raining the whole afternoon.
他说整个下午雨都在一直下。

407
00:16:34.610 --> 00:16:35.410
It was perfect.
这太完美了。

408
00:16:35.410 --> 00:16:38.510
It became a whole bit, which I know we can get to later.
这后来变成了一个贯口般的梗，我知道我们待会儿可以聊到。

409
00:16:38.850 --> 00:16:41.130
But it made the scene that much more fun.
但这让这场戏变得更有趣了。

410
00:16:41.290 --> 00:16:47.350
It's funny because when I first saw it, I asked Randy, did you guys spray down the parking lot with water?
很有意思的是，我第一次看的时候，我问兰迪，你们是不是用水枪把停车场喷湿了？

411
00:16:47.350 --> 00:16:48.270
And he said, no.
他说没有。

412
00:16:48.390 --> 00:16:49.910
That was our rainy day.
那是我们的雨天。

413
00:16:50.190 --> 00:16:51.850
Yes, it was actually raining.
对，当时其实真的在下雨。

414
00:16:51.850 --> 00:16:57.290
And it was one of the only times I filmed on The Office where they didn't care about my hair and makeup.
而且这也是我在《办公室》拍摄期间为数不多的几次，他们完全不在乎我的发型和妆容。

415
00:16:57.550 --> 00:16:59.050
They were just like, let her get wet.
他们就直接说，让她淋湿吧。

416
00:16:59.490 --> 00:17:07.450
Well, I guess after we finished shooting that one day, it was necessary to match that to the rest of the episode.
嗯，我猜在我们结束那天的拍摄后，为了和这集剩下的部分保持连贯，这是必须的。

417
00:17:07.450 --> 00:17:17.810
So, Michael Gallenberg and our construction coordinator, Tim James, and the special effects crew, led by Ron Nary, added plexiglass sheets over all of the office windows.
所以，迈克尔·加伦贝格和我们的施工协调员蒂姆·詹姆斯，以及由罗恩·纳里领导的特效团队，在所有办公室窗户上都加了有机玻璃板。

418
00:17:18.250 --> 00:17:23.310
And they made it rain out every window for the rest of the episode.
并且在接下来的整集里，他们让每一扇窗户外都在下雨。

419
00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:29.150
Well, I think that's so great because I think it would have been weird to have some scenes where it was raining and some not.
嗯，我觉得这太棒了，因为我觉得如果有些戏下雨有些戏不下，会很奇怪。

420
00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:30.750
I like the consistency.
我喜欢这种连贯性。

421
00:17:31.190 --> 00:17:34.590
I also kind of loved it that we never talked about it.
而且我也有点喜欢我们从没讨论过这件事。

422
00:17:34.790 --> 00:17:35.030
Yeah.
对。

423
00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:37.350
Well, remember what you said about how you could hear it?
嗯，还记得你说的关于你能听到雨声的事吗？

424
00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:47.010
I guess that was kind of an issue because our sound mixer, Ben Patrick, could really hear it through the microphones, especially in the back of the talking heads.
我想这确实是个问题，因为我们的混音师本·帕特里克通过麦克风能清楚地听到雨声，特别是在单人访谈镜头的背景里。

425
00:17:47.270 --> 00:17:57.950
So, they tried putting down these big fuzzy mats called horse hairs inside of the metal troughs that the water would drip into and then it would get sucked back up.
所以，他们试着在金属水槽里铺上这些叫做马毛的大型毛茸茸垫子，水会滴进水槽然后被抽回上面去。

426
00:17:57.950 --> 00:18:03.250
And that would just sort of cycle through the window pane to try to quiet the water, but it didn't work 100%.
这样水就会在窗玻璃周围循环流动以试图减小水声，但并没有完全起作用。

427
00:18:03.250 --> 00:18:07.070
So, you can hear the rain in the back of some of these scenes.
所以你可以在其中一些镜头的背景里听到雨声。

428
00:18:07.830 --> 00:18:13.230
Randy also wanted me to tell people that the fuzzy mats are not actually made out of horse hair.
兰迪还想让我告诉大家，这些毛茸茸的垫子其实并不是用马毛做的。

429
00:18:13.390 --> 00:18:14.350
That was my next question.
那这是我的下一个问题。

430
00:18:14.350 --> 00:18:15.350
I said, oh, no.
我说，噢，不。

431
00:18:15.550 --> 00:18:16.070
Oh, no.
噢，不。

432
00:18:16.170 --> 00:18:17.390
Why are they called that?
为什么它们叫这个名字？

433
00:18:17.590 --> 00:18:17.810
Ah!
啊！

434
00:18:18.150 --> 00:18:23.650
Randy said that it's, quote, just another old-timey holdover from early Hollywood.
兰迪说这，引述一下，只是早期好莱坞留下的又一个老式传统。

435
00:18:24.090 --> 00:18:26.890
Well, thank goodness, because I was worried for a second.
谢天谢地，因为我刚才还担心了一会儿。

436
00:18:27.110 --> 00:18:27.910
It's fakie.
是假的。

437
00:18:28.110 --> 00:18:28.790
Fakie hair.
假发。

438
00:18:29.110 --> 00:18:29.750
Fakie hair.
假发。

439
00:18:31.010 --> 00:18:32.450
Well, that's all I got, lady.
好吧，女士，我收集的就这些了。

440
00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:33.990
Well, I loved all of that.
嗯，我喜欢所有这些。

441
00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:36.270
We should probably take a break and then get into this episode.
我们大概应该休息一下，然后进入这集正片。

442
00:18:36.490 --> 00:18:37.230
I think so.
我也这么觉得。

443
00:18:37.390 --> 00:18:39.590
I've invented a new phrase for today.
我今天发明了一个新短语。

444
00:18:40.070 --> 00:18:40.750
Oh, yeah?
哦，是吗？

445
00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:41.270
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

446
00:18:41.470 --> 00:18:42.290
You want to hear it?
你想听吗？

447
00:18:42.390 --> 00:18:42.670
Yeah.
好啊。

448
00:18:53.650 --> 00:18:54.930
Jenna coined a phrase.
珍娜创造了一个新词。

449
00:18:55.250 --> 00:18:59.910
Well, I want you to know, I had my husband make a sting for this episode.
嗯，我想让你知道，我让我丈夫为这集做了一段音效专场。

450
00:19:00.970 --> 00:19:03.010
And I will surprise you with it.
我会用它给你一个惊喜。

451
00:19:03.130 --> 00:19:05.390
Let's take a break, and we'll be back with new boss.
休息一下，我们换个新老板后马上回来。

452
00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:15.010
Attention all new and existing members of the WDNC.
请WDNC所有新老成员注意。

453
00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:18.890
I'm Melanie Sanders, and this is the We Do Not Care Club podcaSt.
我是梅兰妮·桑德斯，这里是“我们不在乎俱乐部”播客。

454
00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:23.110
We got to midlife and realized we just simply do not care much anymore.
我们到了中年，意识到我们真的再也懒得在乎那么多了。

455
00:19:23.110 --> 00:19:31.170
Now, we got to help each other make sense of hot flashes, itchy ears, chin hair, trifling families, brain fog, and bat wings.
现在，我们要互相帮助，去理清潮热、耳朵痒、下巴长毛、讨厌的亲戚、大脑迷雾和蝙蝠袖。

456
00:19:31.410 --> 00:19:34.050
We are not alone, and we will be heard.
我们并不孤单，我们的声音会被听到。

457
00:19:34.070 --> 00:19:35.950
So come join the WDNC.
所以快来加入WDNC吧。

458
00:19:36.170 --> 00:19:41.330
Follow and listen to the We Do Not Care Club podcast with Melanie Sanders wherever you get your podcaSt.
在各大播客平台关注并收听由梅兰妮·桑德斯主持的“我们不在乎俱乐部”播客。

459
00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:53.500
We're going to kick off this episode with a little meeting in the conference room about Michael's 15th anniversary celebration.
我们将以会议室里关于迈克尔十五周年庆典的小型会议来开启本集节目。

460
00:19:53.500 --> 00:19:57.720
And who is in the party planning committee now?
现在谁在派对筹备委员会里？

461
00:19:58.200 --> 00:20:01.040
Jim, Dwight, and Pam.
吉姆、德怀特和帕姆。

462
00:20:01.420 --> 00:20:02.860
Oh, I'm just there to take notes.
哦，我只是去作记录的。

463
00:20:03.060 --> 00:20:04.660
I don't think I'm really in it.
我觉得我其实并不在里面。

464
00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:08.200
Although later, I guess I am throwing out ideas.
虽然过一会儿，我好像也开始提意见了。

465
00:20:08.480 --> 00:20:09.100
You are.
你是有的。

466
00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:09.760
Hmm.
嗯。

467
00:20:09.880 --> 00:20:11.060
How'd I make my way back in?
我是怎么又回去了？

468
00:20:11.060 --> 00:20:12.760
I think Jim wrangled you in.
我觉得是吉姆把你硬拉进去的。

469
00:20:13.160 --> 00:20:14.700
And I'm going to say, traitor.
我要说，叛徒。

470
00:20:17.560 --> 00:20:24.800
Dwight is going to pitch the idea of a 15-minute round of applause followed by a 15-minute moment of silence.
德怀特会提出这样一个点子：来15分钟的热烈掌声，接着是15分钟的默哀。

471
