00:27:32.180 --> 00:27:32.660
and stuff.
之类的来做数学应用题。

626
00:27:32.800 --> 00:27:33.800
I think that's really fun.
我觉得那真的挺有意思的。

627
00:27:33.880 --> 00:27:34.480
I do, too.
我也是。

628
00:27:34.860 --> 00:27:35.160
All right.
好吧。

629
00:27:35.160 --> 00:27:36.620
I still wouldn't be good at it, though.
不过我还是不擅长就是了。

630
00:27:37.120 --> 00:27:38.960
No, because it's still math.
对，因为本质上还是数学。

631
00:27:39.580 --> 00:27:40.060
Bingo.
说得对。

632
00:27:40.540 --> 00:27:42.320
Were you good in math in school?
你上学时数学好吗？

633
00:27:42.320 --> 00:27:47.840
Because I was very good at math in school, and now, I mean, everyone knows my calculator
因为我上学时数学非常好，现在嘛，大家都知道我那个计算器的

634
00:27:47.840 --> 00:27:52.320
story where I tried to add without a calculator for a year, and I don't know.
故事，我曾试过一年不用计算器加法，结果不知道怎么的。

635
00:27:52.380 --> 00:27:53.200
It's left me.
我都忘光了。

636
00:27:53.440 --> 00:27:56.820
Like, I can barely help my 10-year-old with his math homework now.
比如现在我儿子才10岁，他的数学作业我都快辅导不了了。

637
00:27:57.300 --> 00:27:57.780
Well...
呃……

638
00:27:57.780 --> 00:27:58.500
What happened to me?
我这是怎么了？

639
00:27:58.600 --> 00:27:59.720
I mean, I was really good.
我是说，我以前真的很好。

640
00:27:59.960 --> 00:28:04.760
I was like, you know, 98th percentile in the math tests and stuff.
我记得当时数学测试什么的都在第98百分位左右。

641
00:28:04.760 --> 00:28:10.420
I was a solid, like, B student in math, totally fine, all the way up to algebra two, and then
我数学一直是个稳稳的B等生，完全没问题，直到学到代数二，然后

642
00:28:10.420 --> 00:28:14.820
I had the option to take language over trig, and I love language.
我面临选修语言还是三角函数的选择，而我热爱语言。

643
00:28:14.820 --> 00:28:16.480
I love speaking other languages.
我喜欢说不同的语言。

644
00:28:16.840 --> 00:28:22.540
And so, I actually went all the way up to Spanish four, but I was able to opt out of
所以，我其实一直选修到了西班牙语四级，但我当时选择

645
00:28:22.540 --> 00:28:24.460
trig to do language.
放弃三角函数去学语言了。

646
00:28:24.460 --> 00:28:25.320
I loved trigonometry.
我超爱三角函数。

647
00:28:25.620 --> 00:28:26.380
I didn't take it.
我没学那个。

648
00:28:26.440 --> 00:28:31.300
I didn't care for geometry, but I loved trigonometry, algebra, all of that.
我不太喜欢几何，但我喜欢三角函数、代数，所有这些。

649
00:28:31.460 --> 00:28:31.840
Yeah.
是啊。

650
00:28:32.300 --> 00:28:33.480
But it has left me.
但这些知识现在都离我而去了。

651
00:28:35.340 --> 00:28:41.380
Let's get back to the episode, because a gentleman named Charles has arrived, and he would like
让我们回到这一集，因为一个名叫查尔斯的绅士来了，他想要

652
00:28:41.380 --> 00:28:42.220
to speak with Michael.
跟迈克尔谈谈。

653
00:28:42.220 --> 00:28:46.880
So, hold up, but first, I have a very tall plant alert.
所以，等等，但首先，我有一个超高植物警报。

654
00:28:47.340 --> 00:28:48.220
What's happening?
发生什么事了？

655
00:28:48.480 --> 00:28:51.620
We haven't had a plant at reception alert in a long time.
我们好久没有前台植物警报了。

656
00:28:51.880 --> 00:28:53.520
Two minutes, 23 seconds.
两分二十三秒。

657
00:28:53.860 --> 00:28:56.300
This might be Pam's tallest potted plant.
这可能是 Pam 盆栽里最高的一盆。

658
00:28:56.300 --> 00:28:57.900
I just want to go on record.
我只想把这个记录下来。

659
00:28:58.300 --> 00:28:59.380
You know, it's interesting.
你知道，这很有趣。

660
00:28:59.380 --> 00:29:04.300
I was just looking at the watercolor that Morgan did of Pam's plants.
我刚才还在看摩根画的关于 Pam 植物的水彩画。

661
00:29:04.460 --> 00:29:04.720
Yes.
没错。

662
00:29:04.940 --> 00:29:07.740
There is a plant on there that's very, very tall.
上面有一株植物，非常非常高。

663
00:29:07.960 --> 00:29:09.180
It's down in the corner.
它在角落里。

664
00:29:09.180 --> 00:29:12.680
It's so tall, it actually encroaches on one of the other plants.
它太高了，甚至侵占了另一株植物的空间。

665
00:29:12.880 --> 00:29:14.380
Could this be that plant?
这会不会就是那株植物？

666
00:29:14.500 --> 00:29:15.460
Maybe it is.
也许是的。

667
00:29:15.580 --> 00:29:19.460
The watercolor painting of Pam's plants that we're talking about is done by this fantastic
我们刚才提到的那幅 Pam 植物的水彩画，是一位非常棒的

668
00:29:19.460 --> 00:29:19.820
artiSt.
艺术家画的。

669
00:29:19.940 --> 00:29:20.620
Her name is Morgan.
她叫摩根。

670
00:29:20.900 --> 00:29:24.400
You can find her on Instagram, Morgan Giselle Art.
你可以在 Instagram 上找到她，账号是 Morgan Giselle Art。

671
00:29:24.600 --> 00:29:26.520
Morgan G-E-S-E-L-L-A-R-T.
摩根的拼写是 G-E-S-E-L-L-A-R-T。

672
00:29:26.720 --> 00:29:29.140
You guys, she's painted all of Pam's plants.
伙计们，她画了 Pam 的所有植物。

673
00:29:29.300 --> 00:29:31.060
She calls it Beasley's Botanicals.
她称之为比斯利的植物园。

674
00:29:31.420 --> 00:29:36.460
You can get it as a mug, and she was kind enough to gift me with the original watercolor, which
你可以买到印有这个图案的马克杯，而且她非常慷慨地把水彩画原件送给了我，我

675
00:29:36.460 --> 00:29:36.940
I treasure.
非常珍视。

676
00:29:37.140 --> 00:29:37.480
I know.
我知道。

677
00:29:37.500 --> 00:29:38.340
And you know what she did?
你知道她做了什么吗？

678
00:29:38.340 --> 00:29:42.000
She did all of Angela Martin's outfits in a watercolor painting.
她把安吉拉·马丁所有的穿搭都画成了一幅水彩画。

679
00:29:42.140 --> 00:29:43.600
I have it hanging in my bedroom.
我把它挂在我的卧室里。

680
00:29:43.880 --> 00:29:46.340
So yes, there is a very tall plant at reception.
所以，是的，前台确实有一株很高的植物。

681
00:29:47.040 --> 00:29:52.660
I didn't notice the plant, Angela, because my eyes were on Idris Elba entering the room.
我根本没注意到那株植物，安吉拉，因为我的目光全在走进房间的伊德瑞斯·艾尔巴身上。

682
00:29:52.760 --> 00:29:53.020
Yes.
是的。

683
00:29:53.140 --> 00:29:55.100
Sir Charles Minor has arrived.
查尔斯·迈纳爵士来了。

684
00:29:55.280 --> 00:30:00.420
At two minutes, 50 seconds, Angela Martin looks him up and down.
在两分五十秒时，安吉拉·马丁上下打量了他一番。

685
00:30:00.420 --> 00:30:08.460
Michael welcomes him in and says that everybody needs to go into the break room because he
迈克尔迎他进来，并说大家需要去休息室，因为他

686
00:30:08.460 --> 00:30:10.800
has a surprise that he is setting up.
有个惊喜正在筹备。

687
00:30:11.020 --> 00:30:13.440
Yeah, he whispers to Dwight, I have to get the fish ready.
对，他悄悄对德怀特说，我得把鱼准备好。

688
00:30:13.880 --> 00:30:14.320
Yep.
没错。

689
00:30:14.640 --> 00:30:15.080
Gross.
真恶心。

690
00:30:15.460 --> 00:30:15.620
What?
什么？

691
00:30:17.040 --> 00:30:19.620
And now for a segment I'd like to call...
现在进入我称之为……的环节

692
00:30:22.480 --> 00:30:25.300
History in the break room.
休息室里的历史。

693
00:30:26.260 --> 00:30:26.700
What?
什么？

694
00:30:30.190 --> 00:30:30.810
Break room.
休息室。

695
00:30:31.590 --> 00:30:34.610
I made my husband do that like last night in his car.
我昨天晚上让我丈夫在车里这么干过。

696
00:30:34.770 --> 00:30:35.290
You can tell.
听得出来。

697
00:30:35.430 --> 00:30:37.170
I'm like, do it in the car, in the minivan.
我说，在车里录，在面包车里录。

698
00:30:37.170 --> 00:30:38.150
It'll sound better.
听起来会更好。

699
00:30:39.350 --> 00:30:40.830
History in the break room.
休息室里的历史。

700
00:30:40.830 --> 00:30:44.870
So Michael needs Dwight to distract Charles and the group.
所以迈克尔需要德怀特去转移查尔斯和大家的注意力。

701
00:30:45.010 --> 00:30:46.110
They go in the break room.
他们走进休息室。

702
00:30:46.250 --> 00:30:48.930
He bores them with the history of Scranton.
他用斯克兰顿的历史折磨他们。

703
00:30:49.110 --> 00:30:51.770
We only hear one sentence of this.
我们只听到了其中的一句话。

704
00:30:52.030 --> 00:30:55.110
And I also remember Rain had a hard time not laughing.
我也记得雷恩当时很难忍住不笑。

705
00:30:55.210 --> 00:30:59.230
And you can kind of see him starting that twinkle when he starts to break.
你能看出他快要破功时，眼睛里开始闪烁的那种光芒。

706
00:30:59.490 --> 00:31:02.010
Do you know there was a whole entire speech in the script?
你们知道剧本里其实整整有一大段演讲吗？

707
00:31:02.270 --> 00:31:09.870
I do because I remember that Rain had to memorize a huge monologue about the history of Scranton.
我知道，因为我记得雷恩不得不背下一大段关于斯克兰顿历史的独白。

708
00:31:09.870 --> 00:31:13.270
In particular, the anthracite coal mining communities.
特别是无烟煤开采社区的历史。

709
00:31:13.850 --> 00:31:21.730
You guys, when we saw the episode and only one line made it, I just know Rain was like,
各位，当我们看到剧集里只有一句台词保留下来时，我当时就知道雷恩心里肯定在想：

710
00:31:21.990 --> 00:31:22.710
son of a...
操……

711
00:31:22.710 --> 00:31:24.510
This is what he had to learn.
这就是他必须背下来的内容。

712
00:31:24.930 --> 00:31:30.410
Originally founded in 1866, Scranton quickly became one of Pennsylvania's largest anthracite
斯克兰顿最初成立于1866年，很快就成为了宾夕法尼亚州最大的无烟煤

713
00:31:30.410 --> 00:31:31.410
coal mining communities.
开采社区之一。

714
00:31:31.750 --> 00:31:36.430
The nation's thirst for energy during World War II was slacked by the extensive strip mining
二战期间国家对能源的渴求，通过该地区广泛的露天采矿

715
00:31:36.430 --> 00:31:37.710
operations in the area.
作业得到了满足。

716
00:31:37.710 --> 00:31:42.610
But in 1959, the Knox mine disaster all but erased the local mining industry.
但在1959年，诺克斯矿难几乎彻底摧毁了当地的采矿业。

717
00:31:42.870 --> 00:31:47.990
The area was then scarred by abandoned coal mining structures, stripped mines, and slag
此后，该地区布满了废弃的煤矿建筑、露天矿坑和矿渣

718
00:31:47.990 --> 00:31:51.270
heaps, which give mute testimony to the city's industrial paSt.
堆，无声地见证着这座城市工业过去的沧桑。

719
00:31:51.430 --> 00:31:53.110
So anyway, what's up with you?
总之，你最近怎么样？

720
00:31:53.650 --> 00:31:58.090
Can you believe he learned that whole thing and one line made it?
你能相信他把整段都背下来了，结果只用了一句吗？

721
00:31:58.470 --> 00:32:01.730
The first line and the ending line made it.
第一句和最后一句保留下来了。

722
00:32:01.730 --> 00:32:03.170
Oh my gosh.
噢天哪。

723
00:32:04.030 --> 00:32:09.870
Well, then Michael is going to come in and he says, all right, everybody come to the conference
好吧，然后迈克尔走进来，他说，好了，大家来会议

724
00:32:09.870 --> 00:32:10.250
room.
室。

725
00:32:10.470 --> 00:32:14.870
And you know, he does that big gesture where his hand hits the door frame.
你们知道的，他做那个大动作时，手撞到了门框上。

726
00:32:14.970 --> 00:32:17.170
Yeah, he does this windmill like motion.
对，他做了一个风车般的动作。

727
00:32:17.490 --> 00:32:21.910
And then he does the thing that Steve does so well where he's like, oh, right?
然后他做了史蒂夫最拿手的那种动作，就是那种，哦，对吧？

728
00:32:22.010 --> 00:32:23.250
Where he like grunts.
就是他会发出那种哼声。

729
00:32:23.390 --> 00:32:26.810
It was the same thing that cracked me up when he would get out of Pam's chair after it had
这和他在帕姆的椅子陷下去后从上面站起来时，把我逗笑的是同一个动作。

730
00:32:26.810 --> 00:32:27.390
sunk down.
或者是凯文像圣诞老人一样坐在他身上的时候。

731
00:32:27.570 --> 00:32:29.410
Or when Kevin sat on him as Santa.
是同一个声音。

732
00:32:29.410 --> 00:32:30.550
It's the same noise.
就像是，呃。

733
00:32:30.670 --> 00:32:31.230
It's like, ugh.
对，他太擅长这种压抑的呻吟了。

734
00:32:31.590 --> 00:32:34.910
Yeah, he does these suppressed groans so well.
好吧，整个过程都是剧本里写好的。

735
00:32:35.370 --> 00:32:38.090
Well, that whole thing was scripted.
我查了一下，剧本里是这样描写这个细节的。

736
00:32:38.250 --> 00:32:41.550
I looked it up and this is what the script said about that.
上面写着，迈克尔用风车手势招呼大家跟上，但手重重地砸在了入口的

737
00:32:41.690 --> 00:32:47.770
It says, Michael windmill motions for people to follow, but nails his hand on top of the
顶端。

738
00:32:47.770 --> 00:32:48.170
entrance.
他痛得咧嘴。

739
00:32:48.210 --> 00:32:49.190
He winces.
所以这个小细节是为史蒂夫量身设计的，他演得太棒了。

740
00:32:49.510 --> 00:32:53.610
So that little moment was scripted for Steve and he was amazing.
他演得真好，因为你拿不准。

741
00:32:53.890 --> 00:32:55.830
He was amazing because you're not sure.
你搞不清这究竟是他在即兴胡闹，还是真的发生了。

742
00:32:55.830 --> 00:32:59.370
You're not sure if that was just him mucking around or if it really happened.
好吧，一进会议室，迈克尔就要展示一堆

743
00:32:59.610 --> 00:33:05.010
Well, once in the conference room, Michael is going to present an array of bagels that
切成查理斯名字首字母“C”字形的贝果面包。

744
00:33:05.010 --> 00:33:08.590
have been cut into the shape of a C for Charles.
花了他一整晚时间。

745
00:33:08.750 --> 00:33:09.490
Took them all night.
对。

746
00:33:09.670 --> 00:33:09.910
Yeah.
我必须得说，当我看到这一幕时，我觉得这非常有《足球教练》的风格。

747
00:33:10.710 --> 00:33:15.870
I have to say when I saw this, I thought this was a very Ted Lasso move.
你不觉得泰德·拉索

748
00:33:16.450 --> 00:33:18.450
Couldn't you see Ted Lasso?
和比尔德会做出这种事吗？

749
00:33:18.690 --> 00:33:20.590
And Beard doing something like this?
比如把所有的贝果面包做成某个特定的字母。

750
00:33:20.670 --> 00:33:23.750
Like making all the bagels into like a certain letter.
比如把所有的贝果面包做成某个特定的字母。

751
00:33:24.150 --> 00:33:24.970
Am I crazy?
我是疯了吗？

752
00:33:24.970 --> 00:33:26.430
No, it's a Ted Lasso.
不，这是泰德·拉索。

753
00:33:26.530 --> 00:33:27.250
I can see it.
我能看出来。

754
00:33:27.470 --> 00:33:32.730
And this just got my brain sort of thinking about how there are actually a lot of things
这让我的大脑开始联想到，其实有很多事情

755
00:33:32.730 --> 00:33:36.350
that Michael does that Ted Lasso also kind of does.
迈克尔做的事，泰德·拉索也差不多会做。

756
00:33:36.450 --> 00:33:38.270
But he does it better and more appropriate.
但他做得更好，也更得体。

757
00:33:38.530 --> 00:33:41.510
You guys were talking about the show Ted Lasso with Jason Sudeikis.
你们刚才在聊由杰森·苏戴奇斯主演的电视剧《泰德·拉索》。

758
00:33:42.030 --> 00:33:43.690
Bill Lawrence executive produced the show.
比尔·劳伦斯是该剧的执行制片人。

759
00:33:43.810 --> 00:33:44.330
He's amazing.
他太棒了。

760
00:33:44.650 --> 00:33:46.730
It just won a gazillion Emmys.
这部剧刚刚赢得了无数座艾美奖。

761
00:33:46.750 --> 00:33:47.870
The cast is phenomenal.
演员阵容非常强大。

762
00:33:48.510 --> 00:33:52.790
But I was just watching an episode the other day where Ted Lasso is like riding lawnmower
但我前几天刚好看到一集，讲的是泰德·拉索在骑草坪修剪机

763
00:33:52.790 --> 00:33:53.530
with the guy.
和那个人一起。

764
00:33:54.970 --> 00:33:56.390
Did you see Michael Scott doing that?
你看到迈克尔·斯科特做过那种事吗？

765
00:33:56.550 --> 00:33:57.250
Michael and Dwight?
迈克尔和德怀特？

766
00:33:57.630 --> 00:33:57.970
Yeah.
对。

767
00:33:58.710 --> 00:33:59.510
I don't know.
我不知道。

768
00:33:59.630 --> 00:34:02.450
I was seeing some parallels and it was kind of charming me.
我看到了一些相似之处，这让我觉得有点迷人。

769
00:34:02.590 --> 00:34:07.290
And I think also because I thought it was kind of cute that he made the bagels into a C.
而且我觉得也是因为，他把贝果面包摆成字母C的形状，我觉得挺可爱的。

770
00:34:07.530 --> 00:34:08.210
I did too.
我也这么觉得。

771
00:34:08.370 --> 00:34:11.370
It's just that his presentation of it was so sad.
只是他呈献的方式太凄凉了。

772
00:34:11.510 --> 00:34:13.330
It was just on a bunch of paper towels.
就直接放在一堆纸巾上。

773
00:34:13.330 --> 00:34:16.010
Well, and also like just his buildup.
对啊，还有他铺垫的方式。

774
00:34:16.230 --> 00:34:17.930
His buildup was so huge.
他的铺垫做得太大了。

775
00:34:18.150 --> 00:34:18.310
Yeah.
对。

776
00:34:19.410 --> 00:34:19.670
Aw.
啊。

777
00:34:20.050 --> 00:34:23.370
Ted would have had them on a tray and that would have made the difference.
