If you do not like it, then I think there are some bagels left over from this morning.
如果你不喜欢，那我觉得早上还剩了些贝果面包。

1075
00:47:12.760 --> 00:47:13.240
Sass.
傲娇。

1076
00:47:14.100 --> 00:47:15.120
That's major sass.
太傲娇了。

1077
00:47:16.000 --> 00:47:20.700
Well, you know, in the conference room, Kelly's going to say to Angela, should I seduce Charles?
好吧，你懂的，在会议室里，凯莉会对安吉拉说，我要不要去勾引查尔斯？

1078
00:47:21.000 --> 00:47:22.380
And Angela goes, no.
然后安吉拉说，不要。

1079
00:47:22.560 --> 00:47:23.960
No one wants to see that.
没人想看那一幕。

1080
00:47:24.540 --> 00:47:26.780
But then she sneaks a smile at Charles.
但接着她又偷偷朝查尔斯笑了一下。

1081
00:47:27.300 --> 00:47:28.740
I like this rivalry.
我喜欢这种针锋相对。

1082
00:47:29.140 --> 00:47:31.280
Mindy and I had so much fun doing this.
我和敏迪拍这个可开心了。

1083
00:47:31.440 --> 00:47:33.100
We had such a blaSt.
我们玩得太嗨了。

1084
00:47:33.740 --> 00:47:36.360
Michael is trying to call David Wallace again.
迈克尔又在尝试给大卫·华莱士打电话。

1085
00:47:36.700 --> 00:47:41.260
And then we're going to have the scene that is the tipping point for Michael.
然后接下来就是迈克尔的情绪爆发点的那场戏。

1086
00:47:41.540 --> 00:47:43.160
It's so cringy.
太让人脚趾抠地了。

1087
00:47:43.740 --> 00:47:47.920
Kevin approaches Michael and says he used the wrong calendar for his spreadsheet.
凯文走向迈克尔，说他做电子表格时用了错误的日历。

1088
00:47:48.100 --> 00:47:49.080
The wrong calendar.
错误的日历。

1089
00:47:49.400 --> 00:47:50.140
From 2008.
2008年的。

1090
00:47:50.620 --> 00:47:52.740
And he has to redo his spreadsheet.
他得重新做表格。

1091
00:47:52.900 --> 00:47:54.200
Can he come in over the weekend?
他能在周末来加班吗？

1092
00:47:54.740 --> 00:47:56.300
That would mean overtime.
那意味着加班费。

1093
00:47:57.260 --> 00:47:58.480
Michael says yes.
迈克尔说可以。

1094
00:47:58.700 --> 00:47:59.760
Charles says no.
查尔斯说不行。

1095
00:48:00.080 --> 00:48:01.640
No, we talked about this.
不行，我们讨论过这事的。

1096
00:48:01.640 --> 00:48:04.160
And Michael's like, I'm sorry, this is my branch.
然后迈克尔就说，抱歉，这是我的分公司。

1097
00:48:04.160 --> 00:48:05.660
And I like your initiative, Kevin.
我挺欣赏你的积极性，凯文。

1098
00:48:05.820 --> 00:48:06.200
And yes.
可以的。

1099
00:48:06.340 --> 00:48:07.620
And Charles just shuts him down.
结果查尔斯直接驳回了他。

1100
00:48:07.620 --> 00:48:09.920
He's like, that's not how we're going to do this.
他就像是在说，我们可不兴这么搞。

1101
00:48:10.300 --> 00:48:12.080
And how does Michael respond?
迈克尔是怎么回应的？

1102
00:48:12.840 --> 00:48:15.580
Michael starts doing that, like...
迈克尔开始那样做，就像……

1103
00:48:15.580 --> 00:48:16.640
Six-year-old thing.
六岁小孩子的把戏。

1104
00:48:16.800 --> 00:48:19.760
That echo thing where you just repeat what the other person is saying.
那种学别人说话的复读把戏。

1105
00:48:19.760 --> 00:48:20.860
Yeah, I know you are.
对啊，我知道你是。

1106
00:48:20.960 --> 00:48:21.740
I know you are.
我知道你是。

1107
00:48:22.200 --> 00:48:24.620
And then it's like going on and on.
然后这就没完没了地进行下去。

1108
00:48:24.760 --> 00:48:27.100
And everyone in the bullpen is saying, Michael...
大办公室里的每个人都在喊，迈克尔……

1109
00:48:27.100 --> 00:48:28.180
Michael, stop it!
迈克尔，住手！

1110
00:48:28.240 --> 00:48:28.600
Please!
求你了！

1111
00:48:29.220 --> 00:48:34.260
Pam has a talking head where she says she can tell how upset Michael is by which comedy routine he uses.
帕姆有一个单采镜头，她说她能根据迈克尔用的是哪个喜剧桥段，看出他有多生气。

1112
00:48:34.520 --> 00:48:36.880
And how infantile and immature he gets.
以及他变得多么幼稚和不成熟。

1113
00:48:37.300 --> 00:48:40.480
He has skipped over the Ace Ventura butt routine.
他直接跳过了《神探飞机头》的用屁股说话桥段。

1114
00:48:40.720 --> 00:48:42.340
Which never happens.
这绝对不可能发生。

1115
00:48:42.800 --> 00:48:44.220
She knows this is bad.
她知道这情况不妙。

1116
00:48:44.420 --> 00:48:46.760
He skipped over Ace Ventura butt routine.
他跳过了《神探飞机头》的屁股桥段。

1117
00:48:47.280 --> 00:48:48.220
That's the talking butt.
就是那个会说话的屁股。

1118
00:48:48.840 --> 00:48:50.500
Yeah, I know the talking butt.
对，我知道那个会说话的屁股。

1119
00:48:50.780 --> 00:48:51.700
I know it.
我知道。

1120
00:48:52.340 --> 00:48:56.300
He's going to take all that energy and he's going to say, all right, fine.
他要把所有这些精力都用上，然后他会说，好吧，行。

1121
00:48:56.560 --> 00:48:58.880
Party planning committee in the conference room.
派对策划委员会在会议室开会。

1122
00:48:59.320 --> 00:49:03.160
And there was a thing in the script where he was like, you guys just pitch me ideas because
剧本里本来有一段是他说，你们就向我提建议吧，因为

1123
00:49:03.160 --> 00:49:05.620
maybe planning my party will make me feel better.
也许帮我策划派对能让我感觉好点。

1124
00:49:06.140 --> 00:49:07.640
I remember shooting this scene.
我记得拍这场戏的时候。

1125
00:49:07.820 --> 00:49:09.680
We had a hard time getting through it.
我们费了好大劲才拍完。

1126
00:49:09.860 --> 00:49:10.500
I bet.
我敢说肯定是。

1127
00:49:10.660 --> 00:49:11.040
I bet.
我敢说。

1128
00:49:11.460 --> 00:49:16.380
Well, while you guys start pitching party ideas, Charles is going to go over to Phyllis and say,
好吧，在你们开始提派对创意的时候，查尔斯会走到菲莉丝身边说，

1129
00:49:16.380 --> 00:49:17.620
you know, what is the PPC?
你知道的，PPC是什么？

1130
00:49:18.160 --> 00:49:23.940
And Phyllis says, it's the party planning committee and they spend hours planning parties.
然后菲莉丝说，这是派对策划委员会，他们花好几个小时策划派对。

1131
00:49:24.460 --> 00:49:27.060
And then Phyllis would have had a talking head.
然后菲莉丝本来还有一个单采镜头。

1132
00:49:27.180 --> 00:49:29.900
And I so wish it had made it in.
我多希望这段能剪进正片里啊。

1133
00:49:30.320 --> 00:49:32.200
Are you ready for some Phyllis sass?
准备好迎接菲莉丝的毒舌了吗？

1134
00:49:32.580 --> 00:49:33.760
Here's her talking head.
这是她的单采镜头。

1135
00:49:34.620 --> 00:49:35.920
I built that house.
那房子是我建的。

1136
00:49:36.080 --> 00:49:37.300
I can burn it down.
我随时能把它烧毁。

1137
00:49:44.830 --> 00:49:49.050
Oh, I love this side of Phyllis, especially when it's not directed at Angela.
哦，我喜欢菲莉丝这一面，尤其是当这不针对安吉拉的时候。

1138
00:49:50.590 --> 00:49:56.110
Well, in that moment when Charles is talking to Phyllis, at 14 minutes, 48 seconds, you
好吧，在查尔斯和菲莉丝说话的那个瞬间，在14分48秒，

1139
00:49:56.110 --> 00:50:01.150
get a real good shot of this silver insulated coffee mug that he's been carrying around
你能很清楚地看到他一整天都在拿着的那个

1140
00:50:01.150 --> 00:50:01.750
all day.
银色保温咖啡杯。

1141
00:50:02.190 --> 00:50:03.590
Do you know what it said on it?
你知道上面写的是什么吗？

1142
00:50:03.930 --> 00:50:04.290
What?
什么？

1143
00:50:05.010 --> 00:50:05.810
Sadekoy Steel.
Sadekoy Steel。

1144
00:50:06.190 --> 00:50:07.590
Oh, nice detail.
哦，不错的细节。

1145
00:50:07.990 --> 00:50:09.250
Way to go, Phil Shea.
干得漂亮，道具师菲尔·谢。

1146
00:50:09.350 --> 00:50:09.590
Yeah.
是啊。

1147
00:50:09.590 --> 00:50:15.870
Because when Charles enters the conference room, he is holding that Sadekoy Steel coffee
因为当查尔斯走进会议室时，他拿着那个Sadekoy Steel的咖啡杯，

1148
00:50:15.870 --> 00:50:17.930
mug eye level to Michael Scott.
高度正好跟迈克尔·斯科特的眼睛平齐。

1149
00:50:18.170 --> 00:50:19.270
And I don't know.
我不知道。

1150
00:50:19.350 --> 00:50:23.990
I just felt like it was subliminally pissing Michael off.
我只是觉得这在潜意识里把迈克尔气得够呛。

1151
00:50:24.230 --> 00:50:24.850
Just poking the bear.
只是逗逗这头熊。

1152
00:50:24.990 --> 00:50:25.190
Yeah.
是啊。

1153
00:50:25.330 --> 00:50:26.870
Just rubbing it in his face.
就是在他面前炫耀。

1154
00:50:27.330 --> 00:50:29.790
Well, Charles wants to know what the heck they're doing in there.
好吧，查尔斯想知道他们在里面到底在搞什么鬼。

1155
00:50:29.930 --> 00:50:31.790
He now has been tipped off by Phyllis.
他现在被菲莉丝告密了。

1156
00:50:31.890 --> 00:50:33.250
This is a big waste of time.
这纯粹是在浪费时间。

1157
00:50:33.630 --> 00:50:38.670
And he starts to look over Jim's shoulder and he's like, what is a two-way petting zoo?
然后他开始看着吉姆的肩膀说，什么是双向抚摸动物园？

1158
00:50:39.370 --> 00:50:40.790
And Jim is really embarrassed.
吉姆真的觉得很尴尬。

1159
00:50:40.790 --> 00:50:43.710
And he says, you pet the animals, they pet you back.
他说，你抚摸动物，动物也抚摸你。

1160
00:50:43.910 --> 00:50:45.010
We could not get through that.
我们简直没法把它读顺。

1161
00:50:45.650 --> 00:50:48.070
Two-way petting zoo did us in every time.
双向抚摸动物园每次都让我们破功。

1162
00:50:48.510 --> 00:50:50.070
I got a little bit curious.
我有点好奇。

1163
00:50:50.510 --> 00:50:52.510
You did not look up two-way petting zoo.
你不会去查了“双向抚摸动物园”吧。

1164
00:50:52.650 --> 00:50:53.070
I did.
我查了。

1165
00:50:53.410 --> 00:50:53.910
Oh, no.
哦，不。

1166
00:50:54.230 --> 00:50:55.230
Is that at Burning Man?
那是火人节上的吗？

1167
00:50:55.410 --> 00:50:57.730
Because I have a friend who was in a petting zoo at Burning Man.
因为我有个朋友曾在火人节上参加过抚摸动物园。

1168
00:50:58.210 --> 00:50:58.610
What?
什么？

1169
00:50:59.170 --> 00:51:00.250
What is that?
那是什么？

1170
00:51:00.990 --> 00:51:01.830
What is that?
那是什么？

1171
00:51:07.020 --> 00:51:08.020
I did improv with.
我跟她一起做过即兴表演。

1172
00:51:08.600 --> 00:51:12.560
And I'll never forget, you know, she's kind of like a free spirit.
我永远不会忘记，你知道的，她有点像个崇尚自由的人。

1173
00:51:13.100 --> 00:51:14.440
And I was at the airport.
当时我在机场。

1174
00:51:14.640 --> 00:51:15.400
This is years ago.
那是好几年前的事了。

1175
00:51:15.660 --> 00:51:17.460
And I see her running through the airport.
我看到她一路小跑着穿过机场。

1176
00:51:17.680 --> 00:51:21.560
And it looked like she had like, I don't know, she had like a carry-on, but you could
看起来她好像带着，我不知道，她带了一个登机箱，但你能

1177
00:51:21.560 --> 00:51:23.840
see sort of like a onesie poking out of it.
看到里面好像露出了连体衣的一角。

1178
00:51:24.340 --> 00:51:25.220
She's running through the airport.
她正一路小跑着穿过机场。

1179
00:51:25.360 --> 00:51:26.100
I'm like, hi.
我说，嗨。

1180
00:51:26.360 --> 00:51:27.020
And she's like, hi.
她说，嗨。

1181
00:51:27.380 --> 00:51:29.020
And she's like, so good to see you.
她说，很高兴见到你。

1182
00:51:29.120 --> 00:51:29.760
And I was like, you too.
我说，我也是。

1183
00:51:29.860 --> 00:51:30.680
She's like, where are you going?
她说，你要去哪儿？

1184
00:51:30.780 --> 00:51:32.100
And I was like, I'm going to see my folks.
我说，我要去看看我爸妈。

1185
00:51:32.180 --> 00:51:33.100
I said, what about you?
我说，你呢？

1186
00:51:33.600 --> 00:51:35.640
And she said, oh, I'm going to Burning Man.
她说，哦，我要去火人节。

1187
00:51:35.640 --> 00:51:37.880
And I'm in the petting zoo this year.
今年我在抚摸动物园里。

1188
00:51:38.720 --> 00:51:42.760
And so I had to say, what's a petting zoo?
所以我不得不问，什么是抚摸动物园？

1189
00:51:42.980 --> 00:51:46.320
And she was like, well, you know, you dress up as animals and let people pet you.
她说，嗯，你知道的，你打扮成动物，让别人来抚摸你。

1190
00:51:47.500 --> 00:51:47.980
Wow.
哇。

1191
00:51:48.360 --> 00:51:48.620
Yeah.
是啊。

1192
00:51:49.180 --> 00:51:49.660
Yeah.
对。

1193
00:51:50.460 --> 00:51:51.160
I mean.
我是说。

1194
00:51:51.340 --> 00:51:54.120
That's what I thought of when you said that.
你这么说的时候，我想到的就是这个。

1195
00:51:54.120 --> 00:51:56.900
But I did not know that.
但我并不知道那个。

1196
00:51:57.340 --> 00:52:02.160
I mean, I found out that there's no such thing as a two-way petting zoo where actual animals
我是说，我发现根本没有什么双向抚摸动物园，能让真正的动物

1197
00:52:02.160 --> 00:52:02.900
pet the humans.
去抚摸人类。

1198
00:52:02.920 --> 00:52:06.500
But I did not know about this human petting zoo at Burning Man.
但我确实不知道火人节上有这种人类抚摸动物园。

1199
00:52:06.740 --> 00:52:08.640
Did you think animals would pet humans?
你以为动物会抚摸人类吗？

1200
00:52:09.280 --> 00:52:10.280
You know what, lady?
你知道吗，大姐？

1201
00:52:10.400 --> 00:52:11.120
I didn't know.
我不知道。

1202
00:52:11.280 --> 00:52:11.740
I admit.
我承认。

1203
00:52:11.860 --> 00:52:12.880
It was a weird Google.
那次谷歌搜索真够诡异的。

1204
00:52:13.160 --> 00:52:13.400
Yeah.
是啊。

1205
00:52:13.580 --> 00:52:15.060
But I did find this.
但我确实找到了这个。

1206
00:52:15.340 --> 00:52:15.560
What?
什么？

1207
00:52:16.240 --> 00:52:23.860
Two-way petting zoo is apparently like a euphemism for describing like a really
双向抚摸动物园显然就像是一个委婉的说法，用来形容那种非常

1208
00:52:23.860 --> 00:52:27.040
intense, passionate sexual encounter.
强烈、热烈的主动性接触。

1209
00:52:27.700 --> 00:52:33.580
Like you would be like, oh, me and my boyfriend had a real two-way petting zoo last night.
就好像你会说，哦，我和我男朋友昨晚来了一场真正的双向抚摸动物园。

1210
00:52:33.840 --> 00:52:34.740
No, come on.
不是吧，拜托。

1211
00:52:34.800 --> 00:52:35.640
Who talks like that?
谁会那样说话？

1212
00:52:35.900 --> 00:52:39.220
But you are giving me flashbacks of like sixth grade sex ed.
但你让我回想起了六年级性教育课的场景。

1213
00:52:39.480 --> 00:52:42.940
We're like, we had a coach teach us sixth grade sex ed.
我们当时就像，我们有个教练教我们六年级性教育课。

1214
00:52:43.020 --> 00:52:44.980
And he was like, sometimes there's heavy petting.
然后他说，有时候会有激烈的抚摸。

1215
00:52:45.240 --> 00:52:45.720
Sometimes.
有时会有。

1216
00:52:46.120 --> 00:52:46.640
We're like, ah.
我们当时就想，啊。

1217
00:52:49.140 --> 00:52:49.620
Yeah.
是啊。

1218
00:52:50.240 --> 00:52:51.040
I don't know.
我不知道。

1219
00:52:51.260 --> 00:52:55.400
Well, we don't know what Jim meant, but we know he's super embarrassed.
好吧，我们不知道吉姆是什么意思，但我们知道他超级尴尬。

1220
00:52:55.720 --> 00:52:57.160
Well, Charles has had enough.
好吧，查尔斯已经受够了。

1221
00:52:57.300 --> 00:53:00.540
He wants to dissolve the PPC effective immediately.
他想立即解散派对策划委员会。

1222
00:53:01.120 --> 00:53:03.520
This is where Michael completely flips out.
这就是迈克尔彻底崩溃的地方。

1223
00:53:03.720 --> 00:53:08.740
And there was a deleted scene where he made a defensive argument to keep the PPC.
还有一个被删减的片段，他在其中做了辩护来保留派对策划委员会。

1224
00:53:09.200 --> 00:53:10.840
Oh, we need to hear it.
哦，我们得听听。

1225
00:53:11.540 --> 00:53:15.180
The party planning committee is an institution in this institution.
派对策划委员会是这个机构里的一个机构。

1226
00:53:15.340 --> 00:53:21.600
It is something that I incorporated in the mid-90s to celebrate the Laserdisc release of
这是我在90年代中期成立的，为了庆祝《红粉联盟》的

1227
00:53:21.600 --> 00:53:22.440
A League of Their Own.
激光影碟发行。

1228
00:53:22.600 --> 00:53:24.300
It has become a tradition here.
这已经成为了这里的传统。

1229
00:53:24.500 --> 00:53:26.860
It is something that is important to all of us.
这对我们所有人都很重要。

1230
00:53:26.960 --> 00:53:28.640
What did we do for League of Their Own party?
我们当时为《红粉联盟》派对做了什么？

1231
00:53:28.740 --> 00:53:30.540
A pizza of your own party.
属于你自己的披萨派对。

1232
00:53:30.720 --> 00:53:31.480
Make your own pizza.
自己做披萨。

1233
00:53:31.700 --> 00:53:32.680
I didn't even work here then.
我那时候甚至都还没在这里工作。

1234
00:53:32.860 --> 00:53:33.560
I just shared the stories.
我只是分享了这些故事。

1235
00:53:33.960 --> 00:53:34.540
Okay, thank you, Dwight.
好的，谢谢你，德怀特。

1236
00:53:34.620 --> 00:53:36.360
That should take five minutes of one person's day.
这应该只占一个人一天中的五分钟。

1237
00:53:36.520 --> 00:53:36.800
Really?
真的吗？

1238
00:53:36.800 --> 00:53:37.440
Five minutes.
五分钟。

1239
00:53:38.460 --> 00:53:38.940
Yeah.
对。

1240
00:53:39.960 --> 00:53:43.040
And then that's where the scene picks up.
然后这就是场景接续的地方。

1241
00:53:43.140 --> 00:53:46.020
And he just goes off and he's like, you don't even know how paper is made.
他直接爆发了，然后他说，你们甚至都不知道纸是怎么造出来的。

1242
00:53:46.020 --> 00:53:46.980
It's not like steel.
它不像钢铁。

1243
00:53:46.980 --> 00:53:48.200
You don't put it in a furnace.
你不用把它放进熔炉里。

1244
00:53:48.220 --> 00:53:50.700
And he starts to cry.
然后他开始哭泣。

1245
00:53:51.100 --> 00:53:54.320
And he shoves over a chair on his way out.
他在离开的时候推倒了一把椅子。

1246
00:53:54.440 --> 00:53:55.700
That was not in the script.
那不在剧本里。

1247
00:53:56.000 --> 00:53:57.280
He has a whole tantrum.
他发了一通大脾气。

1248
00:53:57.600 --> 00:53:58.760
Ah, I remember.
啊，我想起来了。

1249
00:53:59.340 --> 00:54:03.300
After Michael leaves, Jim is going to attempt to start over with Charles.
迈克尔离开后，吉姆打算重新开始和查尔斯交流。

1250
00:54:03.920 --> 00:54:04.280
Yeah.
对。

1251
00:54:04.920 --> 00:54:06.600
And this created...
而这就创造了……

1252
00:54:06.600 --> 00:54:07.780
Fan mail, fan mail, flurry!
粉丝来信，粉丝来信，雪片般飞来！

1253
00:54:08.500 --> 00:54:09.240
Number two.
第二点。

1254
00:54:09.620 --> 00:54:09.960
Oh.
哦。

1255
00:54:10.460 --> 00:54:13.060
A lot of people wrote in.
很多人写信进来了。

1256
00:54:13.240 --> 00:54:14.320
This is a quote.
这是一段引语。

1257
00:54:14.740 --> 00:54:21.600
I am so excited to finally get to discuss my biggest pet peeve in the whole series.
我非常兴奋，终于能讨论我整部剧里最讨厌的槽点了。

1258
00:54:21.980 --> 00:54:22.860
Oh my goodness.
噢天哪。

1259
00:54:23.400 --> 00:54:23.920
What?
什么？

1260
00:54:24.440 --> 00:54:31.140
At 16 minutes, 40 seconds, Jim says he's a great number two for the office.
在16分40秒时，吉姆说他是办公室非常棒的副手。

1261
00:54:31.900 --> 00:54:35.640
And Charles responds by saying he didn't know that position existed.
查尔斯回应说他不知道还有这个职位。

1262
00:54:35.940 --> 00:54:36.280
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1263
00:54:36.700 --> 00:54:41.740
And then Jim kind of like tap dances and he's like, well, at first it was made up for Dwight,
然后吉姆就有点像是在跳踢踏舞，他说，呃，一开始这是为德怀特虚设的，

1264
00:54:41.880 --> 00:54:43.780
but then, you know, Michael gave it to me.
但后来，你懂的，迈克尔把它给了我。

1265
00:54:44.220 --> 00:54:48.100
And kind of all ends with Charles being like, is this made up position important to you?
最后查尔斯来了一句：这个虚设的职位对你很重要吗？

1266
00:54:48.340 --> 00:54:48.660
Yeah.
是啊。

1267
00:54:50.220 --> 00:54:52.420
Well, people are P.O.ed.
好吧，大家都很生气。

1268
00:54:52.860 --> 00:54:53.460
At who?
生谁的气？

1269
00:54:54.040 --> 00:54:54.880
Here's the thing.
事情是这样的。

1270
00:54:54.880 --> 00:55:01.560
I mean, people sent in lists of evidence to say that this number two position that Jim
我是说，大家寄来了列举证据的清单，力证吉姆

1271
00:55:01.560 --> 00:55:02.640
holds is real.
担任的这个副手职位

1272
00:55:02.920 --> 00:55:06.620
It is not a made up position and that Charles should know that.
是真实存在的，不是虚构的，查尔斯应该知道这一点。

1273
00:55:07.180 --> 00:55:08.340
Here's the evidence.
证据如下。

1274
00:55:08.620 --> 00:55:14.440
In branch closing, Jan is talking to Jim about going back to Scranton and she says, quote,
在《分公司关门》里，简和吉姆谈论回斯克兰顿的事，她说，引述如下，

1275
00:55:14.440 --> 00:55:17.880
we'd like to offer you the number two position at that branch.
我们想提供给你那个分公司的副手职位。

1276
00:55:18.520 --> 00:55:22.780
In the merger, Michael is on the phone with Jan after firing Tony.
在《合并》中，迈克尔在开除托尼后跟简通电话。

1277
00:55:23.040 --> 00:55:26.860
He tries to blame Dwight by saying, bad advice from my number two.
他试图把责任推给德怀特，说，我的副手给出了糟糕的建议。

1278
00:55:27.040 --> 00:55:30.120
And Jan says, Jim is your number two.
简说，吉姆是你的副手。

1279
00:55:30.320 --> 00:55:32.460
I sent you a memo about this.
我给你发过备忘录的。

1280
00:55:32.620 --> 00:55:33.020
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1281
00:55:33.680 --> 00:55:38.360
In the merger, Jim confirms to Dwight that the job comes with a pay raise.
在《合并》中，吉姆向德怀特确认这份工作伴随着加薪。

1282
00:55:38.800 --> 00:55:39.560
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1283
00:55:39.560 --> 00:55:46.140
In Benihana Christmas, when Pam gives her Christmas gift to Jim, he turns it down using, quote,
在《班尼哈娜圣诞节》里，当帕姆把圣诞礼物送给吉姆时，他拒绝了，理由是

1284
00:55:46.320 --> 00:55:48.600
his promotion as an excuse.
他升职了。

1285
00:55:49.300 --> 00:55:55.840
Also in a Benihana Christmas, Dwight refers to himself as the ranking number three and he
同样在《班尼哈娜圣诞节》里，德怀特自称是排名第三，并且他

1286
00:55:55.840 --> 00:56:00.200
finally concedes to Jim's authority as ranking number two.
最终承认了吉姆作为排名第二的权威。

1287
00:56:00.520 --> 00:56:05.580
This is when, you know, they're trying to validate the committee to plan parties.
这就是当他们，你知道的，试图让老派委员会合法化的时候。

1288
00:56:05.820 --> 00:56:06.040
Right.
对。

1289
00:56:06.160 --> 00:56:07.080
They get in this whole argument.
他们为此大吵了一架。

1290
00:56:07.080 --> 00:56:11.860
In the return, Andy tells Jim, I'm thrilled to be working directly beneath you.
在《回归》中，安迪对吉姆说，我很高兴能在你手下直接工作。

1291
00:56:12.000 --> 00:56:16.920
And in women's appreciation, Dwight tells Jim, you may be second in command, but that does
而在《女性赞赏日》中，德怀特对吉姆说，你可能是二把手，但这

1292
00:56:16.920 --> 00:56:18.380
not put you above the law.
并不意味着你凌驾于法律之上。

1293
00:56:18.800 --> 00:56:20.480
This is a real position.
这是一个真实的职位。

1294
00:56:20.480 --> 00:56:25.520
I agree with everybody that, yes, I think Jim doesn't present it well.
我同意大家的看法，是的，我觉得吉姆没表达好。

1295
00:56:25.920 --> 00:56:27.640
And then he gets flustered.
然后他就慌乱了。

1296
00:56:27.840 --> 00:56:28.800
I think so, too.
我也这么觉得。

1297
00:56:29.100 --> 00:56:31.600
By the way, great research, everyone.
顺便说一句，大家做得调查太棒了。

1298
00:56:31.960 --> 00:56:32.380
Yeah.
对。

1299
00:56:32.540 --> 00:56:33.420
I'm very impressed.
我印象非常深刻。

1300
00:56:33.420 --> 00:56:41.000
Let me give a shout out to Laura K., Alexandra K., Cy L., Dan C., Emily M., and others.
我要感谢劳拉·K、亚历山大·K、赛·L、丹·C、艾米莉·M以及其他人。

1301
00:56:41.340 --> 00:56:42.080
Well done.
干得好。

1302
00:56:42.380 --> 00:56:42.980
I like it.
我喜欢。

1303
00:56:42.980 --> 00:56:44.160
People were fired up.
大家的情绪都很高涨。

1304
00:56:44.300 --> 00:56:45.040
I like it.
我喜欢。

1305
00:56:45.180 --> 00:56:46.720
It was a fan mail blizzard.
简直是粉丝来信大雪崩。

1306
00:56:47.000 --> 00:56:47.240
Yeah.
是啊。

1307
00:56:47.800 --> 00:56:49.220
Jim just can't win with Charles.
吉姆在查尔斯面前就是讨不到好。

1308
00:56:49.540 --> 00:56:52.880
There were more scenes where he just got busted throughout the day.
还有更多他整天被抓包的镜头。

1309
00:56:53.100 --> 00:56:54.880
One of them happened at front reception.
其中一个发生在正门前台。

1310
00:56:55.460 --> 00:56:57.500
Oh, I remember shooting this.
哦，我记得拍过这个。

1311
00:56:57.840 --> 00:56:58.860
Can we hear that?
我们能听听那个吗？

1312
00:56:59.300 --> 00:57:00.600
He really doesn't like me.
他是真的很不喜欢我。

1313
00:57:00.860 --> 00:57:02.000
But you look so dapper.
但你看起来真精神。

1314
00:57:02.000 --> 00:57:02.860
Thank you.
谢谢你。

1315
00:57:03.460 --> 00:57:04.800
I'm working so hard.
我工作可努力了。

1316
00:57:05.080 --> 00:57:06.200
I was hitting the phones.
我一直在拼命打电话。

1317
00:57:06.320 --> 00:57:07.140
I closed the sale.
我谈成了业务。

1318
00:57:07.360 --> 00:57:08.020
I updated my contact liSt.
我更新了联系人列表。

1319
00:57:08.020 --> 00:57:08.580
Is he there, Jim?
他在那儿吗，吉姆？

1320
00:57:08.720 --> 00:57:08.900
What?
什么？

1321
00:57:09.240 --> 00:57:09.680
I...
我……

1322
00:57:10.800 --> 00:57:12.900
Hey, go tell him you updated your contact liSt.
嘿，去告诉他你更新了联系人列表。

1323
00:57:13.080 --> 00:57:14.120
I would tell him if it...
我要是告诉他如果……

1324
00:57:16.280 --> 00:57:17.000
You're mocking me?
你在取笑我吗？

1325
00:57:18.160 --> 00:57:18.600
Really?
真的吗？

1326
00:57:18.800 --> 00:57:19.100
Today?
今天？

1327
00:57:19.680 --> 00:57:20.880
Like I don't have enough going on?
就好像我手头的事还不够多似的？

1328
00:57:21.900 --> 00:57:22.680
I'm sorry.
我很抱歉。

1329
00:57:22.820 --> 00:57:23.500
Have a candy.
吃块糖吧。

1330
00:57:24.080 --> 00:57:24.580
Thank you.
谢谢你。

1331
00:57:30.010 --> 00:57:31.870
Sweetie, do you mind eating that at your desk?
亲爱的，你介意在你的办公桌吃那个吗？

1332
00:57:32.250 --> 00:57:34.450
I don't want him to keep seeing us together.
我不想让他一直看到我们在一起。

1333
00:57:36.190 --> 00:57:40.470
Okay, when I had to say that line, could you eat that at your desk?
好吧，当我不得不说那句台词时，你能去你的办公桌吃吗？

1334
00:57:40.470 --> 00:57:41.690
We could not get through that.
我们俩根本演不下去。

1335
00:57:41.870 --> 00:57:47.450
That made John and I laugh so hard that Pam was like, could you just do that somewhere else?
这让约翰和我笑得太厉害了，以至于帕姆说，你们能不能换个地方做这个？

1336
00:57:47.850 --> 00:57:50.470
He also, which you guys can't see it, right?
他还，这个你们大家看不到，对吧？

1337
00:57:50.810 --> 00:57:53.190
It's in the deleted scenes if you have the DVDs.
如果你有DVD的话，它在删除片段里。

1338
00:57:53.430 --> 00:57:59.290
When Pam says that, John, as Jim, looks at the camera like super deadpan like, are you kidding me?
当帕姆说完那句话时，约翰饰演的吉姆面无表情地看着镜头，仿佛在说，你在开玩笑吧？

1339
00:58:00.890 --> 00:58:02.270
I remember all of that.
我都记得。

1340
00:58:02.650 --> 00:58:04.030
I remember it so clearly.
我记得清清楚楚。

1341
00:58:04.730 --> 00:58:06.290
Well, Michael's going to drive to corporate.
好吧，迈克尔要开车去总公司。

1342
00:58:06.530 --> 00:58:09.570
He's going to confront David Wallace as he's leaving the men's room.
他打算在大卫·华莱士从男洗手间出来时堵住他。

1343
00:58:09.850 --> 00:58:11.410
This is a classic Michael move.
这绝对是迈克尔的经典作风。

1344
00:58:11.550 --> 00:58:13.770
I'm sorry, you guys, but Angela did that to me today.
对不起，各位，但安吉拉今天对我也这么做了。

1345
00:58:13.770 --> 00:58:14.290
I did.
我做了。

1346
00:58:14.610 --> 00:58:15.090
I did.
我确实做了。

1347
00:58:15.130 --> 00:58:16.330
I went to the restroom during our break.
我休息的时候去了洗手间。

1348
00:58:16.330 --> 00:58:16.950
Well, there's only...
好吧，只有……

1349
00:58:16.950 --> 00:58:18.850
Okay, first of all, there's only one bathroom here.
好吧，首先，这里只有一个洗手间。

1350
00:58:18.950 --> 00:58:19.690
And one hallway.
而且只有一条走廊。

1351
00:58:19.870 --> 00:58:20.030
Yeah.
是啊。

1352
00:58:20.350 --> 00:58:24.350
But you were right there, and you had this email you wanted to show me.
但你当时就在那儿，而且你有一封想给我看的电子邮件。

1353
00:58:24.450 --> 00:58:26.970
So as soon as she came out of the bathroom, I was like, look at this.
所以她一从洗手间出来，我就说，快看这个。

1354
00:58:27.070 --> 00:58:28.870
And I said, you just Michael Scott-ed me.
然后我说，你刚刚把我“迈克尔·斯科特”了一把。

1355
00:58:28.870 --> 00:58:29.170
Yeah.
对。

1356
00:58:30.970 --> 00:58:34.790
Anyway, David Wallace hears Michael out, and he's like, you know what?
总之，大卫·华莱士听完了迈克尔的解释，然后他说，你知道吗？

1357
00:58:35.050 --> 00:58:38.490
Look, you can have your 15th anniversary party.
听着，你可以办你的十五周年派对。

1358
00:58:38.550 --> 00:58:40.190
You can have the figs.
你可以有无花果。

1359
00:58:40.310 --> 00:58:42.370
Michael keeps talking about these figs.
迈克尔一直在念叨这些无花果。

1360
00:58:42.450 --> 00:58:42.930
I know.
我知道。

1361
00:58:43.170 --> 00:58:44.890
There was a whole fig runner.
甚至还有一个专门摆无花果的桌旗。

1362
00:58:45.070 --> 00:58:45.330
What?
什么？

1363
00:58:45.550 --> 00:58:46.710
Yes, in the script.
对，剧本里写了。

1364
00:58:46.710 --> 00:58:51.290
I thought this was just like a random thing, and I was so tickled by it.
我以为这只是随便写写的东西，当时觉得特别逗。

1365
00:58:51.370 --> 00:58:54.690
I was like, what is his commitment to having figs?
我就想，他对非得有无花果这事儿执念有多深啊？

1366
00:58:54.770 --> 00:58:55.070
Yeah.
是啊。

1367
00:58:55.070 --> 00:58:58.170
So this would have been a callback to an earlier scene.
所以这本来是呼应前面的一场戏。

1368
00:58:58.330 --> 00:59:04.970
When they're doing all the party planning, one of the things Michael wanted was like bacon-wrapped figs.
当他们在策划派对的时候，迈克尔想要的东西之一就是培根卷无花果。

1369
00:59:05.250 --> 00:59:05.650
Okay?
好吗？

1370
00:59:05.990 --> 00:59:10.870
And then remember when he started to spiral out to Charles Minor about canceling the party?
然后还记得当他因为取消派对的事开始在查尔斯·迈纳面前情绪失控吗？

1371
00:59:10.870 --> 00:59:15.150
He had this whole speech where he was like, there will be horse-drawn carriages.
他发表了一大通演讲，内容大概是，会有马车。

1372
00:59:15.310 --> 00:59:17.470
There will be pancetta-wrapped figs.
会有意式烟肉卷无花果。

1373
00:59:17.590 --> 00:59:19.190
There will be breakdancers.
会有霹雳舞者。

1374
00:59:19.710 --> 00:59:20.190
Wow.
哇。

1375
00:59:20.450 --> 00:59:20.710
Yeah.
对。

1376
00:59:21.150 --> 00:59:22.370
Those are the figs.
就是那些无花果。

1377
00:59:22.370 --> 00:59:22.970
The figs.
那些无花果。

1378
00:59:23.070 --> 00:59:24.190
They've already arrived.
它们已经送到了。

1379
00:59:24.330 --> 00:59:24.770
They're arriving.
它们正在送来。

1380
00:59:24.770 --> 00:59:25.810
What's he going to do with them?
他打算拿它们怎么办？

1381
00:59:25.890 --> 00:59:26.370
Exactly.
就是说啊。

1382
00:59:41.030 --> 00:59:41.890
I quit.
我辞职。

1383
00:59:42.410 --> 00:59:43.070
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1384
00:59:43.630 --> 00:59:44.650
He quits.
他辞职了。

1385
00:59:44.910 --> 00:59:46.330
I was so surprised.
我太惊讶了。

1386
00:59:46.630 --> 00:59:47.590
It's amazing.
太绝了。

1387
00:59:47.930 --> 00:59:48.190
Yeah.
对。

1388
00:59:48.590 --> 00:59:51.750
I have a real tangent to throw in here.
我这里要插播一个完全扯远的话题。

1389
00:59:51.970 --> 00:59:52.210
Okay.
行吧。

1390
00:59:52.490 --> 00:59:57.230
I don't know if you noticed, but at the very beginning of the scene, David Wallace is drinking
我不知道你有没有注意到，但在戏刚开始的时候，大卫·华莱士在喝

1391
00:59:57.230 --> 00:59:59.570
water out of a Fiji water bottle.
斐济牌瓶装水。

1392
01:00:00.110 --> 01:00:06.130
It was really random to me because he's turned the bottle in such a way that you can't see
我觉得这挺偶然的，因为他把瓶子转了个角度，让你看不清

1393
01:00:06.130 --> 01:00:08.930
the name facing you, but it's clearly Fiji water.
正面的名字，但那明显就是斐济水。

1394
01:00:09.190 --> 01:00:13.130
And I was so confused because I thought they never let us do that.
我当时好困惑，因为我以为他们从不允许我们这么做。

1395
01:00:13.610 --> 01:00:18.050
And I just wondered, was that he had been drinking some Fiji water and it ended up in
我只是在想，是不是他之前喝了点斐济水，结果落在了

1396
01:00:18.050 --> 01:00:20.650
the scene and he turned, because, you know, was he, I don't know.
片场里，然后他转了转，因为，你知道的，他是不是，我不知道。

1397
01:00:20.710 --> 01:00:22.410
I just, it stood out to me.
我就是觉得这挺显眼的。

1398
01:00:22.410 --> 01:00:29.810
But it also stood out to me because earlier in the week, by coincidence, my family became
但让我觉得显眼，还因为就在周初，很巧的是，我家人开始

1399
01:00:29.810 --> 01:00:32.970
fascinated with the origins of bottled water.
对瓶装水的起源着迷。

1400
01:00:33.270 --> 01:00:37.710
So we're in this phase right now where our 10-year-old, if we're talking at dinner and
所以我们现在正处于这样一个阶段，我们十岁的孩子，如果在晚餐时聊天

1401
01:00:37.710 --> 01:00:41.510
we bring up something, he wants to look it up and find out everything about it.
只要我们提起什么事，他就想去查资料，把所有细节都弄个水落石出。

1402
01:00:41.710 --> 01:00:42.830
I wonder where he gets that.
我真不知道这孩子随谁。

1403
01:00:45.410 --> 01:00:50.450
Well, we were discussing getting new water bottles for school, you know, the reusable
其实吧，我们之前在讨论给学校买新的水杯，你知道的，就是那种可重复使用的

1404
01:00:50.450 --> 01:00:55.590
ones, and this got us on bottled water, and my son ended up doing a whole deep dive for
水杯，结果这就聊到了瓶装水，然后我儿子干脆给我们全家做了一番深入研究，

1405
